+ Parks | North Myrtle Beach, SC Skip to Main Content About Us City Parks / Beach Access Recreation Athletics Events & Programs Search 18th & Edge Pocket Park 41st Avenue South Pocket Park Central Park Cherry Grove Oceanfront Park Cherry Grove Park and Boat Ramp Farmers Market Heritage Shores Nature Preserve Hill Street Park Ingram Dunes Nature Preserve McLean Park Russell Burgess Coastal Preserve Yow Park North Myrtle Beach Park & Sports Complex Home Government Departments Parks & Recreation City Parks / Beach Access Parks Parks 9 1 1 1 18th & Edge Pocket Park Small Pocket Park with Benches and Fountain, quiet green space in the heart of crescent beach great to read your book or have a picnic lunch. Link to page 41st Avenue South Pocket Park The park at 41st Avenue South offers a walkway and detailed garden-style plantings. Link to page Central Park This 20 acre park offers opportunities for passive recreation and supervised child play. Link to page Cherry Grove Oceanfront Park The latest addition to the City’s Park system this wonderful little park offers access to the beach as well as the comfort of restrooms and picnic and common areas. Parking is limited to two handicap spaces but off-site public parking can be found at and near the Sea Mountain street end. Link to page Cherry Grove Park and Boat Ramp This popular fishing spot is located on the Cherry Grove marsh and provides boat access to the marsh and the Atlantic Ocean via Hog Inlet. Within the park is reserved parking for the Heritage Shores Nature Preserve. Link to page Farmers Market Picnic Area with 2 picnic shelters and grassy lawn area Link to page Heritage Shores Nature Preserve Heritage Shores Nature Preserve is one of the most unique parks in the city; created in 2007 with seven (7) acres of walking paths. The park is located on an island that extends into the Cherry Grove Marsh. Link to page Hill Street Park This 2.5 acre neighborhood park serves the residential neighborhoods surrounding Hill Street in Cherry Grove. Link to page Ingram Dunes Nature Preserve Ingram Dunes Nature Preserve has an interpretive ½ mile nature trail with signage. It is the last remaining maritime forest in North Myrtle Beach and has native dunes that are 30 feet tall. Link to page McLean Park Known to locals and visitors alike as the most beautiful park in the community, McLean Park is a 10 acre park with a two acre lake. It is located in the heart of the city. This park is the site of many of the Parks and Recreation Department’s special events. All three of McLean Park’s picnic shelters, gazebo, and meditation garden are available for reservation. Link to page Russell Burgess Coastal Preserve Named for a former City Councilman devoted to preservation and maintenance of the marsh, the Preserve is a scenic overview of the picturesque Cherry Grove Marsh. Created in 2004, the park provides paved parking and foot access to the inlet. A boardwalk was added in 2009 to maintain important Cherry Grove Marsh habitat. Please be aware that fishing and crabbing are permitted from ground level but not from the pier structure. Link to page Yow Park This 1.5 acre neighborhood park serves the surrounding residential areas of Windy Hill. Link to page North Myrtle Beach Park & Sports Complex Link to page --> Contact Us 1030 Possum Trot Road North Myrtle Beach, SC 29582 Phone: 843.280.5570 Popular Pages Fun Zone Special Events Beach Permitting Online Services Sports Complex /QuickLinks.aspx Site Links Home Site Map Copyright Notices Employee Email Employee Login /QuickLinks.aspx Government Websites by CivicPlus® Loading Loading Do Not Show Again Close Arrow Left Arrow Right [] Slideshow Left Arrow Slideshow Right Arrow 
